    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "know, the sad part about what happened to my mother's family when they migrated here is that everyone wants to become Americanized. So they didn't hand down the Polish tradition. So by the time I was born, no one spoke the Polish language at home, but we still went to Bayon to get the kabasa for the holidays and we have three Polish parishes on Staten Island where I grew up. St. Adalba, St. Stannis Lough, and St. Anthony's. So we always went to the Polish churches. And I certainly remember Monica. I'm an only child to a very proud Polish woman. And so my house growing up had photographs of me all over the home. And then in 1978, the College of Cardinals elected John Polasek and a Polish Pope. And my mother took down all the photographs of me and put all the photographs of John Polow up and everybody thought my mother gave birth to the Pope. So it was a very proud moment for all of us.",
