    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "known the president for over 20 years, and he's been very supportive of my elections. Again, we have a great relationship, he endorsed me during my primary, and we won that primary very handedly. But the president also knows that I represent the people of the 11th congressional district, and sometimes things that are good for the rest of the country aren't necessarily good for the people I represent. I had to vote against the tax reform bill because it was going to harm the people I represent. It's going to end up being a tax increase to many of the people I represent. I went to the White House and I sat down with the president and I explained to him why, and he understood. To his credit, he said to me, sometimes you have to go against the party because it's better for the people that you represent. He said, you go vote for the people that you represent, people that sent you here. So I did that with the health care replacement plan as well that would have harmed a lot of our hospital systems here in New York. So I've supported the president and things like national security. I think he's done an incredible job in foreign affairs. Do you certify in the Iran nuclear deal? Look what's happening in North Korea now. They're talking about disarmament. They released our hostages. But he also, I have to represent the people. There's a reason why they call us the House of Representatives. We represent the people who sent us there to be their voice. And I've done that 100% of the time that I've been in Congress.",
