    "turn_text": "No, I think the voters are very smart. I always give the voters incredible credit. You'll find that people will vote for people of different parties on the same ballot. They'll vote for somebody for governor and one party and somebody for Congress and another party. Because I think they're more intelligent than a lot of people give the voters credit for. And they look at not what people say, but what have they done? And for 22 years, I was the deputy borough president after 9-11. Before that, as chief of staff, I helped close the garbage dump on Staten Island. But 12 years as district attorney, Staten Island became the safest community and the safest big city in America. I'm very proud of that. And as of for the last three and a half years, as I've had the honor, I've represented this constituency, this city, with honesty, integrity, and with them and their families in mind. And every time I cast it a vote, what passed a piece of legislation?",
