    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "It is. We're separated by the New York Harbor, and many people go back and forth through the Staten Island Ferry, and sometimes we feel that our local government, not the elected officials in Staten Island, but the local government in City Hall, or the government in Albany, to forget that Staten Island is a great contributor. to this great city and state that we have. And sometimes we have to scream a little bit louder than others to get off voices heard. Back then, when we did close the garbage dump, it ended up we had to sue our good friend Rudy Giuliani. And Rudy Giuliani was a great mayor and a great friend to Staten Island. But we had to sue him to get the garbage dump closed. So there's another example of we have to do what's good for the people that empowered us to lead them in their government, even if it means suing your friend.",
