    "turn_text": "a pathway for legal status for those folks who have come here. Many of those folks, as you and I know, were brought here, I don't say against their will, but they were too young to make a decision. They were brought here by mom and dad. And we're also not a nation that wants to separate families. We're not going to say, all right, that child did nothing wrong. So we're going to let that child stay in this country, but we're going to deport mom and dad who brought that child here. We're not going to do that either. So we have to figure out this. This is a larger debate, but there are smaller measures that we could take to make it easier for people to become citizens here. All of us, all of the folks who you're listening to our show right now, who aren't born here, came here for an opportunity for their families, for their children, came here to contribute to our society, get educated here, start their businesses here, raise their families here with their children, get educated here. Those things we have to allow people to do because it's such a great nation. No one's coming here because it's not a great place to",
